  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "BREAKING - a passing test can turn red on upgrade\n\t\t\t* A call answering with a mock gives a child per address, so The<IChild>() is no longer what the subject received from it: a verification naming the child names the call that reached it, Then<ISink>(_ => _.Accept(The<IParent>().GetChild(1)))\n\t\t\t* Verifying through a step that answered with a real instance is refused, naming the setup to write, where it counted no calls whatever the subject did - a verification that passed with Never now fails\n\t\t\tCHANGED\n\t\t\t* A mocked property keeps its value: a read answers the last set, else what the first read answered\n\t\t\t* Setting a mock's property in a setup lambda is allowed - GuardClause for setters removed\n\t\t\t* A call no setup matches is answered once per address: the same arguments answer the same from then on, other arguments answer otherwise\n\t\t\tFIXED\n\t\t\t* A call answering with a mock gives one per address, so verifying Then<IParent>(_ => _.GetChild(1).Get(9), Once) no longer counts what was called through GetChild(2)",
